  "visualBrief": "Oviedo Cathedral presents three recessed pointed portals and a rose window to the west plaza. The single southern tower rises to a perforated Gothic spire. A tiled nave, chapels and the Cámara Santa exterior connect to the open Museo Catedralicio cloister.",
  "heightPolicy": "The 240 m sea-level datum follows the standard viewer terrain. The tower uses the mapped 80 m height and the three landings follow separately sampled plaza grades.",
  "nativeAxes": "The local +X points east along the fitted precinct frame. A -0.134 rad adjustment in the asset frame follows the long wall edges. The three portals face Plaza de Alfonso II el Casto to the west, with the mapped tall tower on the south side.",
  "limitations": [
    "The cathedral, single tower and connected museum cloister use mapped building outlines. Smaller roofs and facade ornament are exterior photo reconstructions.",
    "The portico is open to the recessed doors. The model depicts the Cámara Santa exterior and the cloister arcade. Interior rooms, relics and carved figures use exterior viewing scale or are outside the model scope."
  ],
